    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="8">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:ICn">I Cn</ref> 8</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="8" corresp="#wit-g-a">And gelæste mann Godes gerihta æghwylce geare rihtlice georne.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="8" corresp="#wit-a">And gelæste man Godes gerihta æghwilce geare rihtlice georne.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="8" corresp="#wit-q">Et reddantur Deo debitę rectitudines annis singulis:</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="8" corresp="#wit-g-a">And gelæste mann Godes gerihta æghwylce geare rihtlice georne.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a">And gelæste mann Godes gerihta æghwylce geare rihtlice georne.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-g-a">And ecclesiastical dues shall be promptly and duly rendered every year.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a">And God’s dues are to be paid readily every year.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Und man leiste gesetzmässig willig Kirchengerechtsame in jedem Jahre:</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And let God's dues be paid lawfully and eagerly every year:</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="291"><ref target="clause:VIAtr_16">VI Atr 16</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 16</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="356"><label>quoted verbatim (bold in Wormald's table)</label> <ref target="clause:VIAtr_16">VI Atr 16–17</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, I Cn 8-8:1: Cn 1018 13-13:3  VI Atr 16-17</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="356"><label>quoted verbatim (bold in Wormald's table)</label> <ref target="clause:Cn-1018_part-030">Cn 1018 13–13.3</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, I Cn 8-8:1: Cn 1018 13-13:3  VI Atr 16-17</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-ppmel" n="18"><label>=</label> <ref target="clause:VAtr_11">V Atr 11</ref> <quote>V Atr 11 = VI 16 = Cn 1018 13 = I Cn 8</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-ppmel" n="18"><label>=</label> <ref target="clause:VIAtr_16">VI Atr 16</ref> <quote>V Atr 11 = VI 16 = Cn 1018 13 = I Cn 8</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-ppmel" n="18"><label>=</label> <ref target="clause:Cn-1018_part-030">Cn 1018 13</ref> <quote>V Atr 11 = VI 16 = Cn 1018 13 = I Cn 8</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-ppmel" n="39"><label>blends</label> <ref target="clause:IIEg_3">II Eg 3–3.1</ref> <quote>only fully blended the two approaches in Cnut's Winchester code (9)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-ppmel" n="39"><label>blends</label> <ref target="clause:VAtr_11">V Atr 11–11.1</ref> <quote>only fully blended the two approaches in Cnut's Winchester code (9)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#kennedy" n="59"><ref target="clause:Cn-1018_part-030">Cn 1018 13–13.4</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">From here D (p. 128) continues with VI Atr 16. Liebermann compares VI Atr 16.</note>
        <note type="translator" source="#rabin-doml">God’s dues: On the dues listed in the following clauses, see the notes to The Laws of Edward and Guthrum 6.1–6.3, Canons 54, and 5 Æthelred 12.</note>
      </div>
